IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `aia-scope`
IMPORT `P2-section-2-gate`

-- P2-art-8: Article 8 (compliance with the requirements) of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act, Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744. Unchanged by the Omnibus.
-- Article 8(1) is the umbrella of Chapter III Section 2: the high-risk AI system complies with the requirements of Articles 9 to 15. It takes the answers of Articles 9 to 15 (each a MAYBE BOOLEAN from its own functions) as a list and
-- adds them up with the combinator of P2-section-2-gate.l4: that is seam S8, the answer the keel's Article 3(20), (23) and (24) take as "the high-risk AI system complies with the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2".
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE the requirement is met on the facts; JUST FALSE the text says no; NOTHING not covered (not applicable on the date asked, or a requirement not answered).

§ `Article 8(1)`

-- src:266 | High-risk AI systems shall comply with the requirements laid down in this Section, taking into account their intended purpose as well as the generally acknowledged state of the art on AI and AI-related technologies.
@ref Art 8(1) first sentence (src:266)
-- The answers of Articles 9 to 15 come in as a list, one MAYBE BOOLEAN for each Article (each Article's own functions, combined by the caller). One requirement not met is the text's own no.
-- The "taking into account" limb: the intended purpose and the generally acknowledged state of the art are taken into account in complying (a plain yes/no input).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the answers of Articles 9 to 15` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the intended purpose and the generally acknowledged state of the art on AI and AI-related technologies have been taken into account` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 8(1) first sentence the high-risk AI system complies with the requirements laid down in this Section` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 8, "", 1)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 all the requirements are met given the answers` `the answers of Articles 9 to 15`
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "High-risk AI systems shall comply with the requirements laid down in this Section"; a requirement of Articles 9 to 15 is not met
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST (`the intended purpose and the generally acknowledged state of the art on AI and AI-related technologies have been taken into account`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "taking into account their intended purpose as well as the generally acknowledged state of the art"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a requirement of Articles 9 to 15 is not answered, or it does not apply on the date asked
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" (seam S14)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) names Articles 9 to 15 and 17 to 25, not Article 8; this branch is not reached for Article 8
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed

-- src:266 | The risk management system referred to in Article 9 shall be taken into account when ensuring compliance with those requirements.
@ref Art 8(1) second sentence (src:266)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the risk management system referred to in Article 9 has been taken into account when ensuring compliance with those requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 8(1) second sentence the risk management system has been taken into account when ensuring compliance with the requirements` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 8, "", 1)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        JUST (`the risk management system referred to in Article 9 has been taken into account when ensuring compliance with those requirements`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The risk management system referred to in Article 9 shall be taken into account when ensuring compliance with those requirements"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed


§ `Article 8(2): products that contain an AI system`

-- src:267 | Where a product contains an AI system, to which the requirements of this Regulation as well as requirements of the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I apply, providers shall be responsible for ensuring that their product is fully compliant with all applicable requirements under applicable Union harmonisation legislation.
@ref Art 8(2) first sentence (src:267)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the product contains an AI system, to which the requirements of this Regulation as well as requirements of the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I apply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider has ensured that the product is fully compliant with all applicable requirements under applicable Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 8(2) first sentence the provider is responsible for ensuring that the product is fully compliant with all applicable requirements under Union harmonisation legislation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 8, "", 2)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        IF NOT (`the product contains an AI system, to which the requirements of this Regulation as well as requirements of the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I apply`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a product contains an AI system, to which the requirements of this Regulation as well as requirements of the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I apply": a duty whose "where" is unmet, fork F-duty-where
        ELSE JUST (`the provider has ensured that the product is fully compliant with all applicable requirements under applicable Union harmonisation legislation`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "providers shall be responsible for ensuring that their product is fully compliant with all applicable requirements under applicable Union harmonisation legislation"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed

DECLARE `Art 8(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 8(2) ensure that the product is fully compliant with all applicable requirements under applicable Union harmonisation legislation`

-- src:267 | Where a product contains an AI system, to which the requirements of this Regulation as well as requirements of the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I apply, providers shall be responsible for ensuring that their product is fully compliant with all applicable requirements under applicable Union harmonisation legislation.
@ref Art 8(2) first sentence (src:267)
-- "providers shall be responsible for ensuring": a duty of the provider with no time limit and no consequence stated, so no trace can show it breached (a late act reads FULFILLED).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the product contains an AI system, to which the requirements of this Regulation as well as requirements of the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 8(2) act`
`Art 8(2) the provider's duty to ensure that the product is fully compliant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 8, "", 2)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        IF `the product contains an AI system, to which the requirements of this Regulation as well as requirements of the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I apply`
        THEN PARTY Provider
             MUST `Art 8(2) ensure that the product is fully compliant with all applicable requirements under applicable Union harmonisation legislation`
             HENCE FULFILLED
        ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the "where" of the sentence is not met
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the Section does not apply on the date asked, or Article 2(2) cuts it off, or Article 2(13) says it may be limited

-- src:267 | In ensuring the compliance of high-risk AI systems referred to in paragraph 1 with the requirements set out in this Section, and in order to ensure consistency, avoid duplication and minimise additional burdens, providers shall have a choice of integrating, as appropriate, the necessary testing and reporting processes, information and documentation they provide with regard to their product into documentation and procedures that already exist and are required under the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I.
@ref Art 8(2) second sentence (src:267)
-- A liberty ("shall have a choice of integrating, as appropriate"). The purposes ("consistency, avoid duplication and minimise additional burdens") are reasons, not conditions.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the documentation and procedures into which the necessary testing and reporting processes, information and documentation would be integrated already exist and are required under the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 8(2) second sentence the provider has the choice of integrating the necessary testing and reporting processes, information and documentation into existing documentation and procedures` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 8, "", 2)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        IF NOT (`the documentation and procedures into which the necessary testing and reporting processes, information and documentation would be integrated already exist and are required under the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "into documentation and procedures that already exist and are required under the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I": the choice is given for those; a grant ("shall have a choice") limited by its own wording
        ELSE JUST (TRUE)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed
